---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Community | The Common Squamish" description="Learn how The Common brings people and local groups together in Squamish through coworking, gatherings, and community support.">
  <header class="page-hd"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow on-dark">Community at The Common</span><h1>The people make<br />this place.</h1><p>Good work matters. So does knowing the people who work beside you.</p></div></header>
  <section class="section light"><div class="wrap split"><div><span class="kicker">The idea behind it</span><h2>Connections with room to grow.</h2><p>The Common was founded to help people and organizations connect. Its early vision took inspiration from the social capital approach of Seats2meet in Utrecht: a shared space becomes more valuable when people share knowledge, make introductions, and help one another.</p><p>That idea is still a useful guide for how this place should feel: welcoming, practical, and open to the people building things in Squamish.</p><a class="inline-link" href="https://www.seats2meet.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read about the original inspiration ↗</a></div><img class="photo" src="/img/approved/shared-table.jpg" alt="Coworkers sharing a table at The Common" loading="lazy" /></div></section>
  <section class="section warm"><div class="wrap community-grid"><article><span class="kicker">Around the table</span><h2>Meet people here.</h2><p>The Common has brought members together through informal socials and shared lunches. The kitchen and communal tables give those small connections somewhere to happen.</p></article><article><span class="kicker">Beyond the building</span><h2>Support local ideas.</h2><p>Community groups, entrepreneurs, and nonprofit gatherings have been part of The Common’s story. For current opportunities to collaborate or use the space for an event, tell us what you have in mind.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/contact/">Get in touch ↗</a></article></div></section>
  <section class="section light"><div class="wrap"><div class="program-intro"><span class="kicker">Part of The Common’s story</span><h2>Ways this place has given back.</h2><p>The original site described three community initiatives. Their current terms and availability should be confirmed before anyone applies.</p></div><div class="program-grid"><article><h3>Common Capital</h3><p>An exchange of time, skills, and connections that could make desk space more accessible for people contributing to the community.</p></article><article><h3>Community grants</h3><p>Support for local groups bringing people together around entrepreneurship and innovation in Squamish.</p></article><article><h3>Venue sponsorship</h3><p>Help for community and nonprofit gatherings that need a place to meet.</p></article></div><p class="program-link">Interested in working together? <a class="inline-link" href="/contact/">Tell us about your idea ↗</a></p></div></section>
  <section class="section warm"><div class="wrap history"><span class="kicker">From our early years</span><h2>A few stories that shaped The Common.</h2><div class="history-grid"><article><span>2017</span><h3>Making room for community</h3><p>In an early note to members, Peter wrote openly about the work of turning a new coworking space into a real community. Member socials and conversations were part of that effort from the start.</p></article><article><span>2018</span><h3>Bringing Squamish together</h3><p>The Common hosted an all-candidates air hockey tournament in the 2018 local election season, with proceeds supporting Howe Sound Women’s Shelter. It was a playful example of the space acting as a local gathering place.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section light"><div class="wrap split"><img class="photo" src="/img/approved/courtyard.jpg" alt="The Common outdoor courtyard" loading="lazy" /><div><span class="kicker">Come see for yourself</span><h2>A place to belong while you get things done.</h2><p>You can start small: book a desk, meet someone for coffee, or ask about membership. We’ll help you find your way in.</p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/day-pass/">Book a desk ↗</a></div></div></section>
</Base>
<style>.split h2,.community-grid h2,.program-intro h2,.history h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,3.5vw,3.2rem);letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:.8rem 0 1rem}.split p,.community-grid p,.program-intro p,.program-grid p,.history p{font-size:1.07rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1.2rem}.community-grid,.history-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:clamp(2rem,5vw,5rem)}.community-grid article,.history-grid article{border-top:2px solid var(--forest);padding-top:1.5rem}.history-grid{margin-top:2rem}.history-grid span{color:var(--accent);font-weight:700}.history-grid h3{font-size:1.35rem;margin:.4rem 0}.program-intro{max-width:780px;margin-bottom:2rem}.program-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1.2rem}.program-grid article{border:1px solid var(--line);background:#fff;padding:1.6rem}.program-grid h3{font-size:1.35rem}.program-link{margin:1.5rem 0 0}@media(max-width:700px){.community-grid,.history-grid,.program-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
